<$fill $name="body">

!! Q: I changed a date and the count did not change.

The counts are a snapshot. It refreshes on reload, on ↻, after an action and when an edit is saved: closing an area card, leaving edit mode, Save/Duplicate/Delete in a form, "+ area", "+ tab", rename, move, delete. Nothing runs while you type: edit a tiddler (a date, a status) and the counts stay until you click ↻.

!! Q: An item I expected is missing.

It may sit in an earlier area (first match wins), be muted (see the footer of the panel), or have a blank or non-date value in the area's date field (`wf-days` drops those).

!! Q: The dock shows `!`.

The area filter is broken. Hover the `!` to see the error. The other areas still work.

!! Q: I drag a row and no ring opens.

No action matched this item. An action needs `wf.group`, and its `wf.filter` must return something for the item. Without a filter it always matches.

!! Q: An action has no tile for a value like `+1d`.

Values with `+` or `-` must be bracketed in `wf.tiles`: `[[today]] [[+1d]]`.

!! Q: The action failed halfway; is it undone?

No. Actions are not transactional. A failing action shows a notice and leaves no mark, but what it changed before the failure stays.

!! Q: I defined a group or action twice.

With the same `wf.name` (group or recipe) the first one found wins. To override a shipped one, use the same //title// as the shadow; your tiddler then replaces it.

!! Q: Move does the wrong default.

A group's default tile is the group's `wf.default` action. When it has several tiles, `wf.default-value` picks one. Move uses the day strip's `+1d` (Tmrw). The day strip rolls forward from today (Today, Tmrw, then the next three weekdays, then +1 wk), so on a Sunday it reads Today, Tmrw (Mon), Tue, Wed, Thu, +1 wk.

!! Q: Does clicking an item close the panel?

No, so you can triage several. A click outside closes it, and that click still reaches what is underneath.

!! Q: I installed it and nothing changed.

JS modules need a server restart (`click-outside.js`, `ring-layer.js`, `date-operators.js`, `live-filter.js`, `live-widget.js`, `datalist.js`, …).

!! Q: The dock is hidden behind the sidebar button.

At `top-right` it can sit under the Vanilla sidebar toggle. Use another corner or move the dock.

!! Q: Tiles are cut off on a small window.

With 5 or 6 groups, a viewport of about 440 px height or less can clamp tiles. Use a taller window.

!! Q: The card says 12 but the dock chip says 9.

The card count is the raw filter count: no first-match placement (an earlier area may claim an item), drafts counted. The dock shows the snapshot after the checks.

!! Q: I dropped a card outside the panel and TiddlyWiki opened its import dialog.

Cards are draggable tiddlers; dropping one on the page is an import. Cancel the dialog. Drop cards on a tab, on another card or on "+ area".

!! Q: Where is the Save button of an area?

There is none. A card edits the area tiddler directly. Actions and groups use a form with Save, which edits a copy.

!! Q: I deleted a shipped action and it is still listed.

Delete on a shipped action or group hides it (`wf.hidden: yes`). Open it from the settings tab or the ring (hidden tiles are dimmed) and press "↺ Shipped" to restore it.

!! Q: I switched the recipe and old fields remain.

Switching keeps the previous recipe's `wf.*` fields in the tiddler, so switching back loses nothing. Remove them in the tiddler editor if you want it clean.

!! Q: How do I clear the default of a group?

"Default of group" in the action form can only set one. Clear it in the group form.

!! Q: Replaces shows one title but `wf.replaces` has several.

The form edits a single title. Edit the field in the tiddler editor for a list.

!! Q: Esc does not close the panel.

Esc steps back in this order: menu, form, pinned ring, open card, edit mode, panel. Press it again.

!! Q: The ring stays open after I release.

In edit mode the ring is pinned. Esc, a click outside, or leaving edit mode closes it.

